12
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
"Can't Help Falling in Love" is a song written by Hugo Peretti, Luigi
Creatore, and George David Weiss and published by Gladys Music, Inc.

13
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:41,000
The melody is based on "Plaisir d'amour", a popular French love
song composed in 1784 by Jean-Paul-Égide Martini.

14
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:16,000
The song was initially written from the perspective of a woman as "Can't Help Falling in Love with Him",
which explains the first and third line ending on "in" rather than words rhyming with "you".

15
00:53:45,000 --> 00:53:51,000
Recorded by singer and actor Elvis Presley, it was part of the album Blue
Hawaii (1961), the soundtrack to the movie Blue Hawaii.

16
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
The song was recorded subsequently in the 1960s by Perry Como, the Lennon Sisters,
Doris Day, Patti Page, Andy Williams, Al Martino and Keely Smith.

17
01:00:55,000 --> 01:01:01,000
In the 1970s, the song was recorded by Marty Robbins, Bob Dylan, the
Stylistics, Shirley Bassey, and Engelbert Humperdinck.

18
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Through the decades, European artists, including Swedish pop group A-Teens, and British reggae and pop group
UB40, recorded their own versions, and grunge band Pearl Jam has covered it at their concerts.

19
01:08:05,000 --> 01:08:11,000
Newer versions continue to be recorded by newer artists, such as Kacey Musgraves
who recorded a version in 2022 for a movie about Elvis Presley.

20
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
This song was ranked one of the greatest songs of
all-time by Rolling Stone Magazine.

